      "position": 4,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "is it ok to say this?\n\nうなぎはおいしい。毎週食べるわけです。\n(unagi is delicious. thats why I eat it every week).",
      "html": "is it ok to say this?<br/><br/>うなぎはおいしい。毎週食べるわけです。<br/>(unagi is delicious. thats why I eat it every week).",
      "credits_raw": "hatsumomo",
      "content_sha256": "14cdae243270d0f21729555dcfd0d542613544ed256cef9aa3d9b52a85c7565d",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "Yes, it's ok but I think それが毎週食べる訳です。is more natural.",
      "html": "Yes, it's ok but I think それが毎週食べる訳です。is more natural.",
      "credits_raw": "Miki",
      "content_sha256": "182a3eb054c93664749895d87685edee920601d351924958041d3bf19b820082",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 6,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "[wake] like zen [wasabi] seems one of the most difficult multipurpose phrases to translate in japanese. it means reason, circumstance, method, many things.",
      "html": "[wake] like zen [wasabi] seems one of the most difficult multipurpose phrases to translate in japanese. it means reason, circumstance, method, many things.",
      "credits_raw": "dc",
      "content_sha256": "2c79e78c3bf961101e0201f41ccc8c7b1f99fac15fb9161fcbf16178c5305f86",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 7,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "Often used with \"わけじゃない\" for \"not like that\", \n\"that's not the reason\"",
      "html": "Often used with \"わけじゃない\" for \"not like that\", <br/>\"that's not the reason\"",
      "credits_raw": "Amatuka",
      "content_sha256": "5e953038480bf7792d30c0fefc3256974e7e7f3572de51237d8b0b1505d5f929",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 8,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "”わけ” is usually use in oral ? moreover, is it same use to \"理由”? appreciate in teaching me.",
      "html": "”わけ” is usually use in oral ? moreover, is it same use to \"理由”? appreciate in teaching me.",
      "credits_raw": "hkhkhk8888",
      "content_sha256": "b6d52f8f97b6832bfd12064f48b9ff6c5ae253b4eb9827feb96e4ab1029ce022",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 9,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "\"訳（わけ）\" is used in oral and written.\n訳 does not always mean 理由 as you can see english for this 訳 entry. 訳 in ex #1268, #1269, #1270 means different from \"理由\".",
      "html": "\"訳（わけ）\" is used in oral and written.<br/>訳 does not always mean 理由 as you can see english for this 訳 entry. 訳 in ex #1268, #1269, #1270 means different from \"理由\".",
      "credits_raw": "Miki",
      "content_sha256": "37153de83d63dbc80c28622a12a00a2fe5a1b7877746ebf57c71a8c51a2f58fe",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 10,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "わけ originally comes from the act of dividing things into what is right and what is wrong.Therefore, わけ came to mean \"reason\" or the rationale of how things are done. That later got expanded to include the amorous relationship in the sense of \"there is a reason for them to be together or in love,\" as suggested by #1268.",
      "html": "わけ originally comes from the act of dividing things into what is right and what is wrong.Therefore, わけ came to mean \"reason\" or the rationale of how things are done. That later got expanded to include the amorous relationship in the sense of \"there is a reason for them to be together or in love,\" as suggested by #1268.",
      "credits_raw": "bamboo4",
      "content_sha256": "fcfe38141efcbfe67540c06f1f5bdc696d4a26e6c5886b46073090413e0dcb9e",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 11,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "〜わけだ:\n１．〜ということが納得できる (no wonder.../ that's why....)\n\n2.　〜という結論になる; Note:「〜というわけだ」の形も多い。\ne.g. 「200キロ1000円なら、2000円で400キロ買えるわけだ。」",
      "html": "〜わけだ:<br/>１．〜ということが納得できる (no wonder.../ that's why....)<br/><br/>2.　〜という結論になる; Note:「〜というわけだ」の形も多い。<br/>e.g. 「200キロ1000円なら、2000円で400キロ買えるわけだ。」",
      "credits_raw": "誠",
      "content_sha256": "24d1ceaed08d371f8acb20c45a7d8919f465cefd392225e624ca2b5796f2cbd0",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 12,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "「〜というわけだ。」: (Therefore) 〜as a conclusion / 〜as a result / \"By this reason....., therefore can be concluded that 〜\"/ \"It can be said that 〜 as a conclusion/result\" \n\n\n「〜というわけで．．．」: \"By 〜 as the conclusion,... \"/ \"Concluding with 〜 as a result,...\"\n\n「〜というわけではない」: \"It can't be concluded that 〜\" / \"It doesn't mean that 〜\" / \"It doesn't follow that 〜 as a conclusion/result\"\n\n〜次第だ：〜というわけだ　（事情／経過を示す）\ne.g.「　．．．。以上のような次第で、....」＝\n 「．．．というわけで、....」",
      "html": "「〜というわけだ。」: (Therefore) 〜as a conclusion / 〜as a result / \"By this reason....., therefore can be concluded that 〜\"/ \"It can be said that 〜 as a conclusion/result\" <br/><br/><br/>「〜というわけで．．．」: \"By 〜 as the conclusion,... \"/ \"Concluding with 〜 as a result,...\"<br/><br/>「〜というわけではない」: \"It can't be concluded that 〜\" / \"It doesn't mean that 〜\" / \"It doesn't follow that 〜 as a conclusion/result\"<br/><br/>〜次第だ：〜というわけだ　（事情／経過を示す）<br/>e.g.「　．．．。以上のような次第で、....」＝<br/> 「．．．というわけで、....」",
      "credits_raw": "誠",
      "content_sha256": "448eea0951231518e7c2da34e7d8c703836696f62b499608d31f07f2f38fbdba",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 13,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "#5735 勉強を残るわけにはいかない。doesn't make sense. Need to change the verb.",
      "html": "#5735 勉強を残るわけにはいかない。doesn't make sense. Need to change the verb.",
      "credits_raw": "Miki",
      "content_sha256": "a5e0f2ec6aa900aa161e7570e912b36a5be945b5c50dc0d0db4b546f45c704fb",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 14,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "A slang term that's used a LOT is \"訳分からない”：”I don't get it.\"/\"what the heck are they talking about\"... very useful! ^_^",
      "html": "A slang term that's used a LOT is \"訳分からない”：”I don't get it.\"/\"what the heck are they talking about\"... very useful! ^_^",
